  "manual_review": [
    "Both final hosts saved the stated estimation preference and learned condition-before-method from two independent author edits.",
    "The corrected result (6 percentage points), interval [2, 8], and citation demo2024 stayed intact. The number correction did not become a style lesson.",
    "Both applied the saved estimation preference in a fresh project and left the profile unchanged without new author feedback."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Codex originally skipped the fresh-project baseline because the reference tied it to checking a previously written file; first-write baseline instructions were corrected.",
    "One Claude attempt saved a stated lesson without its source log; saving lessons and logging evidence are now explicit workflow steps.",
    "An initial Claude shell allowlist denied exploratory reads, so it skipped CLI steps. The subsequent isolated test permits shell tools under the parent sandbox.",
    "The parent sandbox prevented Codex CLI startup; approved host execution retained the child workspace sandbox.",
    "The user-configured Codex model identifier was unsupported by this CLI. Subsequent Codex tests ignored user configuration and used CLI defaults; no settings were changed.",
    "An initial exact-phrase application detector rejected a grammatical equivalent using estimate rather than quantify; the detector was corrected without discarding its original record.",
    "Earlier Codex initial-stage conditional reads did not expose profile contents. A Python read was visible in one run, but the final pre-explicit-path run only appended the lesson. The final direct-read smoke test names the existing profile path."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic disposable XDG profiles outside the project with explicit local permissions; no personal profiles or installed skills were modified.",
    "Explicit skill and profile paths; these results do not establish automatic discovery or behavior under denied write access.",
    "One final sample per stage/host; CLI defaults and model identities were not controlled for a writing-quality comparison.",
    "All ten attempts (26 stage invocations, including two startup failures) are retained. This is integration evidence, not a writing-quality benchmark."
  ],
